## 6. RL seed uncertainty

### 6.1 Why this is required

Deep RL results are seed-sensitive. A single seed can look excellent while the policy family is unstable. Stage B is not credible if it promotes `seed 0` without paired seeds.

### 6.2 Minimum and preferred seed counts

```text
minimum Stage B: 5 paired seeds
preferred promotion discussion: 10 paired seeds
finalist stress confirmation: 10+ seeds if compute permits
```

Paired means:

```text
same seed IDs for candidate and matched baseline;
same train/validation split;
same cost scenarios;
same evaluation script;
same environment version.
```

If `ETHUSDT 4h + SAC + tech_stat seed 0` is the only survivor, it is **not** a Stage B promotion candidate. It is a candidate for paired Stage B reruns.

### 6.3 Recommended seed-level estimators

Report all of:

```text
mean
median
20% trimmed mean
IQM / interquartile mean
paired win rate
probability of improvement
bootstrap confidence interval for paired delta
worst-seed delta
best-minus-median concentration
performance profile
```

Use median and IQM as primary summaries because they are less sensitive to one lucky seed.

### 6.4 Paired bootstrap design

Two levels are needed:

1. **Seed bootstrap:** resample paired seed IDs.
2. **Time/block bootstrap within seed:** resample contiguous or stationary blocks of return differentials.

Practical Stage B bootstrap:

```text
outer: resample seeds with replacement
inner: stationary bootstrap return-differential blocks within each selected seed
statistic: median or IQM of seed-level metrics
reps: 5000 for final report, 1000 for smoke test
```

### 6.5 Probability of improvement

For each seed:

```text
delta_seed = metric(candidate_seed) - metric(matched_baseline_seed)
```

Estimate:

```text
P_improvement = P(delta > 0)
```

from paired seed bootstrap.

Suggested interpretation:

| `P_improvement` | Interpretation            | Policy                                           |
| --------------: | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
|       `>= 0.90` | Strong seed-level support | Promotion-eligible if other gates pass.          |
|     `0.75–0.90` | Borderline                | More seeds or stronger family evidence required. |
|        `< 0.75` | Weak                      | Do not promote.                                  |

### 6.6 Performance-profile reporting

Create performance profiles over seed-level normalized scores:

```text
score = candidate_metric / max(abs(baseline_metric), epsilon)
```

or use paired delta distribution if ratios are unstable. Report the empirical CDF of scores/deltas. This makes it visible whether the candidate improves broadly or only through a tail seed.

### 6.7 Handling seed 0 strong but seeds 1 and 2 weak

Decision:

```text
No promotion.
```

Required next action:

```text
Run the predeclared paired seed set to at least 5 seeds.
If median seed fails or paired win rate is weak, kill or keep exploratory.
If variance remains high after 5 seeds, expand to 10 seeds or demote.
```

Do not say “seed 0 found the good policy.” That is seed selection unless a seed-selection procedure was pre-registered and counted.

### 6.8 Seed report table template

```text
