## 7. Go / no-go thresholds

### 7.1 Conservative default hard gates

A candidate may be considered for Stage C only if all hard gates pass.

| Gate                 |                                    Conservative default | Gate type                    | Rationale                                    |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------: | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Stage C untouched    | No file/row/prompt at `>= 2025-01-01` used before final | Hard                         | Protects held-out firewall.                  |
| Ledger mapping       |                        Valid immutable run-ledger entry | Hard                         | No audit trail, no evidence.                 |
| Return trace         |                         Complete ordered per-step trace | Hard                         | Required for all statistics.                 |
| Matched baseline     |          Present for same seed/split/cost/config family | Hard                         | Avoids leaderboard-only claims.              |
| Paired seeds         |                               `>= 5`; `>= 10` preferred | Hard for Stage B promotion   | Prevents lucky-seed promotion.               |
| Median net return    |         Positive and beats matched baseline after costs | Hard                         | Rejects one-seed or zero-cost illusions.     |
| Median Sharpe        |                                    Positive after costs | Hard                         | Avoids negative-risk-adjusted candidates.    |
| DSR                  |                                     `DSR_N_raw >= 0.95` | Hard for clean promotion     | Corrects multiple testing and non-normality. |
| DSR borderline       |                              `0.80 <= DSR_N_raw < 0.95` | Warning / more evidence      | Not enough for clean promotion.              |
| PBO                  |     `<= 0.10` clean; `0.10–0.20` warning; `>0.20` block | Hard/warning                 | Measures selection instability.              |
| SPA                  |                      `p <= 0.10` minimum family support | Warning/hard depending claim | Family-level data-snooping control.          |
| White RC             |                        `p <= 0.10` conservative support | Warning                      | RC may be conservative.                      |
| Cost stress          |     Survives base and at least one pessimistic scenario | Hard                         | Prevents cost-fragile alpha.                 |
| Synthetic validation |                        Not used as tradability evidence | Hard                         | Project policy.                              |
| Trial ledger         |             Reconstructable `N_raw`; failures disclosed | Hard                         | Required for DSR and RC/SPA.                 |

### 7.2 Warning gates

Warnings do not automatically block, but must be disclosed and usually require more seeds/data:

```text
1. DSR_N_eff passes but DSR_N_raw is borderline.
2. PBO-lite used instead of full fold retraining.
3. White RC fails but SPA passes.
4. Only 5 seeds available.
5. High turnover relative to baseline.
6. Performance concentrated in one regime.
7. Candidate wins on return but worsens drawdown materially.
8. Pessimistic-cost performance remains positive but advantage is mostly erased.
9. Family has too few alternatives for RC/SPA to be very informative.
```

### 7.3 Hard blockers

```text
1. Any Stage C contamination.
2. Missing return_trace_file.
3. Missing ledger entry.
4. Missing matched baseline.
5. Fewer than 5 paired seeds for promotion.
6. Best-seed-only improvement.
7. DSR_N_raw < 0.80.
8. PBO > 0.20, unless candidate is explicitly downgraded to exploratory.
9. Candidate wins only before costs.
10. Candidate fails pessimistic cost scenario.
11. Synthetic-only metric used as evidence.
12. Trial count excludes inspected failures.
13. Family test performed after deleting poor alternatives.
14. PPO/SAC/DQN hyperparameters changed inside Stage B comparison.
```

