## 8. Failure modes and reviewer countermeasures

### 8.1 Data snooping

Failure pattern:

```text
Many feature/source/synthetic variants are tried; the survivor is treated as if it was pre-specified.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
complete trial ledger;
DSR with N_raw;
White RC / SPA over family manifests;
PBO/CSCV rank degradation;
full disclosure of killed, failed, blocked, and diagnostic variants.
```

### 8.2 Seed cherry-picking

Failure pattern:

```text
Seed 0 wins; other seeds are absent, weak, or ignored.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
paired seed set;
median/IQM/trimmed mean;
paired bootstrap CI;
probability of improvement;
seed concentration flag.
```

### 8.3 Cost fragility

Failure pattern:

```text
Candidate wins at zero/base cost but collapses under realistic fees, spread, slippage, funding, or turnover.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
base and pessimistic cost scenarios;
turnover decomposition;
cost-adjusted return traces;
trade-level cost file;
fragility report.
```

### 8.4 Synthetic data misuse

Failure pattern:

```text
Synthetic-only performance is used as evidence, or synthetic data leaks into validation/Stage C.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
synthetic_origin flag;
real-validation-only promotion;
no synthetic rows in validation;
synthetic variants counted as training-protocol trials;
Stage C hard firewall.
```

### 8.5 Stage C leakage

Failure pattern:

```text
2025+ data used for feature fitting, scaler fitting, generator fitting, threshold tuning, prompt context, or report calibration.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
forbidden path manifest;
row-level timestamp audit;
max_input_timestamp <= decision_ts;
no artifact with fit_end >= 2025-01-01;
Stage C access log;
fail-closed validator.
```

### 8.6 Revised or misaligned data

Failure pattern:

```text
Macro/cross-source features use revised values or forward-filled values that were not available at decision time.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
as-of/vintage metadata;
release timestamp fields;
point-in-time merge tests;
prefix recomputation tests;
bar-action timing contract.
```

### 8.7 Derived-feature leakage

Failure pattern:

```text
Rolling features use centered windows, future bars, or validation-fitted normalization.
```

Countermeasures:

```text
prefix-only recomputation test;
train-only scaler hashes;
feature warm-up masks;
max feature lookback registry;
remove validation and verify train features remain unchanged.
```

